# libtasn1 -- the ASN.1 parser GnuTLS and p11-kit read certificates with.
#
# First of the crypto wave. Nothing in the desktop calls it directly; it is
# underneath everything that parses an X.509 certificate. p11-kit's trust
# module uses it to read the CA anchors, and GnuTLS uses it for every
# certificate it validates -- which is what makes enterprise Wi-Fi (802.1X with
# client certificates) work in the Network panel.
#
# Not an LFS package, so it is pinned here rather than in versions.env.
# BLFS 12.4 pins 4.20.0, and the book is the authority for the desktop stack.
SRC_URL=https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/libtasn1/libtasn1-4.20.0.tar.gz
SRC_SHA256=92e0e3bd4c02d4aeee76036b2ddd83f0c732ba4cda5cb71d583272b23587a76c
SRC_DIR=libtasn1-4.20.0

# --disable-static IS LOAD-BEARING HERE, which is worth stating because the
# identical flag in pkgs/npth/pkg.env explicitly is NOT. configure reports
#
#     --enable-static[=PKGS]  build static libraries [default=yes]
#
# so unlike npth -- where libtool already defaulted to shared-only and the flag
# merely pinned it -- omitting this really would ship a libtasn1.a. Nothing in
# finish_install prunes .a files (it drops *.la and usr/share/info/dir), so it
# would reach the published package. install.sh asserts the absence rather than
# trusting the flag, per the rule about asserting outcomes.
#
# NOT PASSED: --disable-doc. Documentation generation is on by default and stays
# on. It needs makeinfo, which texinfo provides and which is packaged; help2man
# is NOT packaged, but configure wraps it in AM_MISSING_PROG (configure.ac:57),
# whose whole purpose is to warn and continue when the generated file is already
# present in the tarball -- and libtasn1 ships its man pages pre-built. Named
# here because "documentation" is the reflex thing to disable after an unrelated
# failure, and disabling it would be a guess rather than a fix.
#
# NOT PASSED: --enable-gtk-doc. Already `default=no`, and gtk-doc is not
# packaged. Recorded so a later reader does not add it looking for API docs.
CONFIGURE_ARGS="--disable-static"
